.TH RUSTFETCH 1 "November 2026" "rustfetch 0.1.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rustfetch, rfetch \- blazing-fast, memory-safe system information fetch tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rustfetch
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B rfetch
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBRustFetch\fR is a lightweight, fast system information tool written in pure Rust.
Designed as a memory-safe alternative to Neofetch and Fastfetch, its core telemetry is
gathered directly from Linux kernel interfaces (\fB/proc\fR, \fB/sys\fR, and stat
syscalls) without spawning shell sub-processes.
.PP
Collectors that have no kernel interface may invoke bounded external tools: package
manager fallbacks (for example \fBrpm\fR), the GitHub update check (\fBcurl\fR or
\fBwget\fR), and the optional sound, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, and media modules (\fBwpctl\fR,
\fBnmcli\fR/\fBiw\fR/\fBiwgetid\fR, \fBbluetoothctl\fR, \fBplayerctl\fR). Those calls
are timeout-bounded and skipped when the tool is absent.
.PP
The executable is also available under the alias \fBrfetch\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General and output
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information, including the cat-breed codename.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIPATH\fR"
Load configuration from \fIPATH\fR instead of the XDG discovery path.
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Output system information as structured JSON.
.TP
.BR \-\-waybar
Output a single-line Waybar/Polybar JSON object.
.TP
.BR \-\-format " \fIFORMAT\fR"
Select the output format: \fIwaybar\fR or \fIjson\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-benchmark
Run an execution profiler that reports microsecond-level latency per collector.
.TP
.BR \-\-live
Run the continuous live monitor with CPU and RAM sparklines and hot theme/border keys.
.TP
.BR \-\-clear ", " \-C
Clear the terminal screen and scrollback before drawing.
.TP
.BR \-\-center
Horizontally center the output in the terminal.
.TP
.BR \-\-separator " \fISEP\fR"
Override the delimiter between label/icon and value.
.TP
.BR \-\-icon-only
Hide text labels and print only icons and values.
.TP
.BR \-\-color " \fICOLOR\fR"
Override the module/key color (a color name such as \fIcyan\fR or a hex value such as \fI#33aadd\fR).
.SS Layout and logo
.TP
.BR \-\-preset " \fINAME\fR"
Apply a built-in layout preset. Available presets: \fBdefault\fR, \fBminimal\fR,
\fBclean\fR, \fBdots\fR, \fBcard\fR, \fBbrackets\fR, \fBneofetch\fR, \fBretro\fR,
\fBmodern\fR, and \fBcompact\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-theme " \fINAME\fR"
Apply one of the 13 built-in color themes (see \fB\-\-list\-themes\fR).
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-logo " \fIDISTRO\fR"
Override the built-in ASCII logo (for example \fIarch\fR, \fIubuntu\fR, \fIfedora\fR,
\fIvoid\fR, or a cat mascot). Run \fB\-\-list\-logos\fR for all keys.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-image " \fIPATH\fR"
Render an image logo instead of ASCII art.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-logo
Disable the logo completely.
.TP
.BR \-\-logo\-position " \fIPOSITION\fR"
Placement of the logo. ASCII logos support \fIleft\fR, \fIright\fR, \fItop\fR,
\fIbottom\fR, and \fIbehind\fR. Image logos support \fIleft\fR (default), \fItop\fR, and
\fIbehind\fR; requesting \fIright\fR or \fIbottom\fR with an image prints a warning and
falls back to \fIleft\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-protocol " \fIPROTOCOL\fR"
Image protocol: \fIauto\fR, \fIkitty\fR, \fIsixel\fR, \fIiterm\fR, \fIbraille\fR, or \fIhalfblock\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-width " \fICOLS\fR"
Image or 3D canvas width in terminal columns.
.TP
.BR \-\-height " \fIROWS\fR"
Image or 3D canvas height in terminal rows.
.TP
.BR \-\-ascii " \fIPATH\fR"
Use a custom static ASCII art file as the logo.
.TP
.BR \-\-border
Enable the decorative box container.
.TP
.BR \-\-border\-style " \fISTYLE\fR"
Box style: \fIrounded\fR, \fIlight\fR, \fIheavy\fR, \fIdouble\fR, \fIdashed\fR,
\fIblock\fR, \fIascii\fR, or \fIbrackets\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-border\-color " \fICOLOR\fR"
Border color (name or hex value).
.TP
.BR \-\-border\-title " \fITITLE\fR"
Title embedded in the top border line.
.TP
.BR \-\-border\-image " \fIPATH\fR"
Use an image file as a decorative border/frame.
.TP
.BR \-\-border\-image\-width " \fICOLS\fR"
Column width of the border image (1 to 512).
.TP
.BR \-\-border\-image\-height " \fIROWS\fR"
Row height of the border image (1 to 512).
.TP
.BR \-\-border\-image\-offset\-x " \fICOLS\fR"
Horizontal offset in columns for a background border image.
.TP
.BR \-\-border\-image\-offset\-y " \fIROWS\fR"
Vertical offset in rows for a background border image.
.TP
.BR \-\-border\-image\-z\-index " \fIINDEX\fR"
Border image stacking z-index (when text_on_top is false).
.TP
.BR \-\-border\-image\-position " \fIPOSITION\fR"
Border image placement: \fIbehind\fR/\fIbackground\fR, \fIleft\fR, \fIright\fR,
\fItop\fR, \fIbottom\fR, or \fIframe\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-border\-image\-protocol " \fIPROTOCOL\fR"
Border image graphics protocol: \fIauto\fR, \fIkitty\fR, or \fIhalfblock\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-border\-image\-preserve\-aspect\-ratio " \fIBOOL\fR"
Preserve border image aspect ratio (\fItrue\fR or \fIfalse\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-border\-image\-text\-on\-top " \fIBOOL\fR"
Draw card text on top of a background border image (\fItrue\fR or \fIfalse\fR).
.SS 3D engine and ASCII animation
.TP
.BR \-\-3d
Enable the real-time 3D animated logo.
.TP
.BR \-\-speed " \fIFLOAT\fR"
3D rotation speed (0.05 to 10).
.TP
.BR \-\-rotate\-x
Rotate the 3D model around the X axis.
.TP
.BR \-\-rotate\-y
Rotate the 3D model around the Y axis.
.TP
.BR \-\-size " \fIFLOAT\fR"
3D model scale (0.1 to 3.0).
.TP
.BR \-\-depth " \fIFLOAT\fR"
3D relief depth (0.1 to 5).
.TP
.BR \-\-shading\-mode " \fIMODE\fR"
Rasterization mode: \fIascii\fR, \fIblocks\fR, \fIsextants\fR, \fIbraille\fR,
\fIdot\fR, \fIwireframe\fR, or \fIsolid\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-shading " \fICHARS\fR"
Custom shading character ramp.
.TP
.BR \-\-frames " \fIN\fR"
Stop after \fIN\fR frames.
.TP
.BR \-\-fps " \fIFPS\fR"
Target frame rate for the 3D engine or ASCII animation.
.TP
.BR \-\-hold
Keep the animation running instead of exiting on the first keypress.
.TP
.BR \-\-exit\-on\-key
Exit the animation on any keypress.
.TP
.BR \-\-infinite
Loop the animation indefinitely.
.TP
.BR \-\-ascii\-anim " \fIPATH\fR"
Play a multi-frame ASCII animation (delimiter-separated file or a frame directory).
.SS Configuration and discovery
.TP
.BR \-\-dump\-config
Print the active, merged configuration (preset + config file + CLI overrides) to stdout.
.TP
.BR \-\-print\-default\-config
Print the commented default configuration template.
.TP
.BR \-\-generate\-config
Write a default \fIconfig.toml\fR into \fI~/.config/rustfetch/\fR, backing up an existing file.
.TP
.BR \-\-import\-fastfetch
Import an existing Fastfetch configuration and convert it to RustFetch TOML.
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-modules
List all 39 supported module names.
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-themes
List all 13 built-in color themes with previews.
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-presets
List all 10 layout presets.
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-logos
List all 38 built-in ASCII logos.
.TP
.BR \-\-clean\-cache
Clear cached module data in \fI~/.cache/rustfetch\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-doctor
Run system, terminal graphics, config validity/warning, cache, and update diagnostics.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-update\-check
Skip the GitHub update check for this run (\fB\-\-doctor \-\-no\-update\-check\fR is fully offline).
.TP
.BR \-\-self\-update ", " \-\-update
Update RustFetch in place via the official one\-line installer
(\fBinstall.sh\fR), checking both GitHub Releases and upstream \fImain\fR
\fICargo.toml\fR while preserving \fIconfig.toml\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-setup ", " \-\-tui
Launch the interactive configuration wizard.
.TP
.BR \-\-init " \fISHELL\fR"
Print the shell startup/resize init snippet for \fIbash\fR, \fIzsh\fR, or \fIfish\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-install\-hook
Install the shell startup/resize hook as a marked block in the shell rc file.
.TP
.BR \-\-uninstall\-hook ", " \-\-remove\-hook
Remove the marked RustFetch hook block from the shell rc file.
.TP
.BR \-\-completions " \fISHELL\fR"
Generate shell completions for \fIbash\fR, \fIzsh\fR, \fIfish\fR, \fIelvish\fR, or \fIpowershell\fR.
.SH MODULES
RustFetch supports 39 canonical module names, listed by \fB\-\-list\-modules\fR:
.PP
\fBSystem:\fR os, os_age, host, board, kernel, uptime, packages, shell, desktop, font,
terminal, locale, processes, init, container, update, custom, break, divider.
.PP
\fBHardware:\fR cpu, cpu_usage, temp, gpu, dgpu, igpu, gpu_driver, memory, swap, disk,
battery, power_profile, brightness, display.
.PP
\fBMedia:\fR sound, media, bluetooth.
.PP
\fBNetwork:\fR wifi, net_io, local_ip.
.PP
Notable behaviour: \fBkernel\fR reads \fI/proc/version\fR; \fBdisplay\fR parses EDID
(header, checksum, four detailed timing descriptors, CTA-861 extensions) from
\fI/sys/class/drm\fR; \fBnet_io\fR uses the default-route interface and reports a
throughput rate when re-run within 10 seconds; \fBbreak\fR and \fBdivider\fR are aliases
that draw a section divider line.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The TOML configuration lives at \fI~/.config/rustfetch/config.toml\fR (or
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rustfetch/config.toml\fR). A top-level \fBpreset\fR key selects a
built-in preset as the base layer; explicit \fB[general]\fR and \fB[[modules]]\fR values
override it. Unknown keys, unknown module names, unknown themes, and out-of-range values
are clamped or ignored and reported by \fBrustfetch \-\-doctor\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set to a non-empty value, ANSI color codes are disabled.
.TP
.BR FORCE_COLOR ", " CLICOLOR_FORCE
When set to a non-empty value other than \fI0\fR, they override \fBNO_COLOR\fR and force colors on.
.TP
.B TERM
When set to \fIdumb\fR, ANSI formatting is stripped. When set to \fIlinux\fR (Linux
virtual console), hex colors are mapped to the 16 standard ANSI colors.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " HOME
Locate the configuration file.
.TP
.BR XDG_CACHE_HOME ", " HOME
Locate the module/update cache.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure (unreadable config, failed self-update, failed hook installation, and similar).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error reported by the command-line parser.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustfetch/config.toml
Main user configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustfetch/logos/
Directory for custom ASCII logo files.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/rustfetch/
Cached module data and update-check metadata.
